From 7e6e2ffe3ec6b3a2ae9f21f2ea79cbb2b14dd7d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:34:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(app): judge the first traverse of a 3+2 plane against
 the machine table

A 3+2 plane read no machine table, so a head-tilt clearance plane that
drops under the table top inside the travel passed. The law now reads the
table's top face over the stated travel when the head tilts. It does not
read the table when only the work tilts (each tilting rotary turns the
part), because the table stays under the work there. A mounted machine
that states no travel gives a note that names the table as not judged.

Fixes #2987

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
